{"title":"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the largest real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and any real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae21bd4bf9cee6f09b70d1f0af125fca9174fa0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />, the following inequality holds:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b064612e98d033faee6fa01a15cd663eb4c1140.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n \\sum_{j=1}^n(n-|j-i|) x_i x_j \\geq C \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i^2\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b18997f1e970086cc0f15649cb581e897aa71d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_n=\\left(\\begin{array}{cccccc} n &amp; n-1 &amp; n-2 &amp; \\cdots &amp; 2 &amp; 1 \\\\ 1 &amp; n &amp; n-1 &amp; \\cdots &amp; 3 &amp; 2 \\\\ 2 &amp; 1 &amp; n &amp; \\cdots &amp; 4 &amp; 3 \\\\ \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\vdots \\\\ n-2 &amp; n-3 &amp; n-4 &amp; \\cdots &amp; n &amp; n-1 \\\\ n-1 &amp; n-2 &amp; n-3 &amp; \\cdots &amp; 1 &amp; n \\end{array}\\right)\\]\" width=\"376\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p>The problem simplifies to finding the smallest real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72fc6cd84c1b6d79703d844553f852946a8ede3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\mathbb{N}^*$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and any vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/7098a56da6633733abfb7a962077712f335258c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />, the following inequality holds:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968049c1b791004d6e4a0a87895176c9ac9d5212.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^T A_n x \\geq C x^T x\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>In other words, find the real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d2e61e90d784129e2cff251b5609ac44b4ef69c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[C \\leq \\inf _{n \\in \\mathbb{N}^*} \\inf _{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n x}{x^T x}\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"51\" />\nGiven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is not easily invertible directly, but is invertible (as it is a sparse matrix):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b9d2bc2760d8a96033f6ac795e03b9a6862b73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_n^{-1}=\\left(\\begin{array}{cccccc} \\frac{n+2}{2 n+2} &amp; \\frac{1}{2} &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; 0 &amp; \\frac{1}{2 n+2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} &amp; 1 &amp; \\frac{1}{2} &amp; \\cdots &amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; -\\frac{1}{2} &amp; 1 &amp; \\frac{1}{2} &amp; \\cdots &amp; 0 \\\\ \\vdots &amp; \\vdots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\ddots &amp; \\vdots \\\\ 0 &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; -\\frac{1}{2} &amp; 1 &amp; \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2 n+2} &amp; 0 &amp; \\cdots &amp; 0 &amp; -\\frac{1}{2} &amp; \\frac{n+2}{2 n+2} \\end{array}\\right)\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"141\" />\n</p><p>Since the inverse has non-zero entries:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3e80969ef7ba6722b29de31c3306a74400780f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\inf _{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n x}{x^T x}=\\left(\\sup _{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n^{-1} x}{x^T x}\\right)^{-1}\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"68\" />\n</p><p>For the eigenvalues <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />&#160;:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea853aa670803bda9679382c5cf004bc76327987.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2 n+2} \\leq \\mu-1 \\leq \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2 n+2}\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d1ca35fdddf39087f194873973ca2828ff287b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 \\leq \\mu \\leq 2\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />\nGiven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/7456fb9e94bd6cd46571ff05816824cb62c56c2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"21\" /> is invertible, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68935d2f37dda4e0ac9ecb1aaca45556320e0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, therefore:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0bdf3077f7dc144b265c60f5a060af1185ede7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{gathered} 0&lt;\\mu \\leq 2 \\\\ \\sup _{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n^{-1} x}{x^T x} \\leq 2 \\end{gathered}\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"79\" />\n</p><p>For a specific <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1ee09ca353fbdf42bf070b84cbd4e3afab2fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\in \\mathbb{R}^n, y=[1,-1,1,-1, \\ldots]^T \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"280\" height=\"22\" />, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b7a24f0b4122452656b6fd1e8efa2a61063064.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{gathered} y^T y=n \\\\ y^T A_n^{-1} y= \\begin{cases}2(n-2)+\\frac{2(n+2)}{n+1} &amp; \\text { if } n \\text { is even } \\\\ 2(n-1) &amp; \\text { if } n \\text { is odd }\\end{cases} \\\\ \\sup _n \\sup _{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n x}{x^T x} \\geq \\sup _n \\frac{y^T A_n y}{y^T y} \\geq 2 \\end{gathered}\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"143\" />\n</p><p>In conclusion:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/470bdc8363e495beff43e8dc4c70f164b0f0a724.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\inf _{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n x}{x^T x}=\\inf _n\\left(\\sup _{\\substack{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n^{-1} x}{x^T x}\\right)^{-1}=\\left(\\sup _{\\substack{n \\\\ n \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\\\ x \\neq 0}} \\frac{x^T A_n^{-1} x}{x^T x}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"508\" height=\"80\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the maximum value of the real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~dalian xes|szm\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA)\">2023 CMO(CHINA)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2023\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CMO(CHINA)_Problems_and_Solutions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"CMO(CHINA) Problems and Solutions\"> All CMO(CHINA) Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018023549\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 177/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1038/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6819/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.737      1 Template:CMO_box\n100.00%    6.737      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27735:|#|:idhash